      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Your own mark; lands with the one authored motion, the ink press.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-reviewed\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.2 8.6l3 3 6.6-7.2\"/></svg><span>Reviewed</span></span>",
      "css": ".ds-reviewed{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;font-family:Archivo,\"Arial Narrow\",sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-weight:800;font-size:13px;color:#47433b;border:2px solid #47433b;border-radius:3px;padding:4px 9px 4px 6px;transform:rotate(2.5deg);animation:ds-press .32s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-reviewed svg{width:15px;height:15px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.2;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}@keyframes ds-press{from{transform:rotate(2.5deg) scale(1.5);opacity:0;filter:blur(2px)}to{transform:rotate(2.5deg) scale(1);opacity:1;filter:none}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-reviewed{animation:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Exhibit Tag",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "exhibit-tag",
      "description": "Luggage-tag label that files an exhibit or a brief.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-tag\"><i class=\"ds-hole\"></i>Exhibit E-01</span>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-family:Archivo,\"Arial Narrow\",sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-weight:800;font-size:13px;padding:3px 10px 3px 7px;border:1px solid #47433b;border-radius:3px 12px 12px 3px;background:#f8f6f0;color:#1c1b18}.ds-hole{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;border:1.5px solid #47433b;background:#f1ede3}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Action",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "action",
      "description": "An exhibit's light action with its key hint.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-act\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.2 8.6l3 3 6.6-7.2\"/></svg><span>Stamp reviewed</span><kbd>x</kbd></button>",
      "css": ".ds-act{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:Archivo,\"Arial Narrow\",sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#1c1b18;background:#f8f6f0;border:1px solid #c9bfab;border-radius:3px;padding:6px 10px;cursor:pointer}.ds-act:hover{border-color:#47433b}.ds-act:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-act:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #1c1b18;outline-offset:2px}.ds-act svg{width:14px;height:14px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.6;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.ds-act kbd{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:11px;color:#6b6559;border:1px solid #ddd5c4;border-radius:3px;padding:0 4px;text-transform:none}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Spine",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "spine-tab",
      "description": "The kraft tab spine: view switch, P-tabs with tilted ink chips, the exhibit index.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-spine\"><div class=\"ds-view\"><button aria-checked=\"true\">All exhibits</button><button aria-checked=\"false\">Needs thought <b>10</b></button></div><div class=\"ds-tab ds-p2\"><span>P2</span><b>1</b></div><a class=\"ds-row ds-here\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-ix\">E-01</span><span>strip.ts:250</span></a><div class=\"ds-tab ds-p3\"><span>P3</span><b>13</b></div><a class=\"ds-row\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-ix\">E-02</span><span>strip.ts:4</span></a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-spine{width:232px;background:#c9a56b;color:#2e2412;padding:16px 0;box-shadow:inset -8px 0 14px -10px rgba(0,0,0,.25)}.ds-view{display:flex;margin:0 12px 16px;border:1px solid #5b4728;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden}.ds-view button{flex:1;border:0;background:transparent;color:#2e2412;font:700 12.5px Archivo,sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;padding:6px 4px;cursor:pointer}.ds-view button[aria-checked=\"true\"]{background:#2e2412;color:#c9a56b}.ds-tab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 14px 5px 18px;font:800 14px Archivo,sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;background:color-mix(in oklab,#b48f55 70%,#c9a56b);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;width:calc(100% - 14px);margin:6px 0 4px}.ds-tab span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.ds-tab span::before{content:\"\";width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px;transform:rotate(-6deg);background:var(--chip)}.ds-p2{--chip:#e57a00}.ds-p3{--chip:#b98f00}.ds-tab b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-row{display:flex;gap:8px;padding:3px 12px 3px 18px;font:11.5px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:#2e2412;text-decoration:none}.ds-row:hover{background:color-mix(in oklab,#2e2412 8%,transparent)}.ds-row.ds-here{background:color-mix(in oklab,#2e2412 14%,transparent)}.ds-ix{color:#5b4728}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Frame with Pinned Line",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "evidence-frame",
      "description": "A code block with hue-free syntax, a marked line in the exhibit's ink and its leader-ruled pin.",
      "html": "<figure class=\"ds-ev\" style=\"--ink:#e57a00\"><div class=\"ds-ev-head\"><span class=\"ds-ev-kind\">Source</span><code>mod/strip.ts:402–405</code></div><div class=\"ds-code\"><div class=\"ds-row\"><span class=\"ds-no\">401</span><span class=\"ds-src\">): N =&gt; {</span></div><div class=\"ds-row ds-mark\"><span class=\"ds-no\">402</span><span class=\"ds-src\">  <b>const</b> state = stripState(view)</span><span class=\"ds-leader\"></span><span class=\"ds-pin\">E-01</span></div><div class=\"ds-row\"><span class=\"ds-no\">403</span><span class=\"ds-src ds-com\">  // one reading of the run</span></div></div></figure>",
      "css": ".ds-ev{margin:0;border:1px solid #ddd5c4;border-radius:3px;background:#f8f6f0;overflow:hidden;max-width:560px}.ds-ev-head{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd5c4;background:#f1ede3;font-size:12.5px}.ds-ev-kind{font:800 11.5px Archivo,sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#6b6559}.ds-code{font:12.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;padding:6px 0;color:#1c1b18}.ds-row{display:flex;align-items:baseline;padding-right:12px}.ds-no{width:44px;padding-right:10px;text-align:right;color:#6b6559;opacity:.75}.ds-src{white-space:pre;padding-left:4px}.ds-src b{font-weight:650}.ds-com{color:#6b6559;font-style:italic}.ds-mark{background:color-mix(in oklab,var(--ink) 16%,#f8f6f0);box-shadow:inset 3px 0 0 var(--ink)}.ds-leader{flex:1 0 24px;align-self:center;border-bottom:1px dashed color-mix(in oklab,var(--ink) 70%,transparent);margin:0 6px 0 14px}.ds-pin{font:800 11px/1 Archivo,sans-serif;font-stretch:72%;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#f8f6f0;background:var(--ink);padding:3px 6px 2px;border-radius:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Diff Rows",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Hue-free diff bands: neutral tint and bold sign for added, paler tint and strike-through for removed.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-diff\"><div class=\"ds-d ds-del\"><span class=\"ds-s\">−</span><span>// so a count of cells is no width there.</span></div><div class=\"ds-d ds-add\"><span class=\"ds-s\">+</span><span>const drawn = site.surface === \"terminal\" ? undefined : el.Svg</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-diff{font:12.5px/1.6 ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;border:1px solid #ddd5c4;border-radius:3px;background:#f8f6f0;padding:6px 0;max-width:560px}.ds-d{display:flex;gap:6px;padding:0 12px;white-space:pre}.ds-s{width:16px;color:#6b6559}.ds-add{background:#ebe6d9;color:#1c1b18}.ds-add .ds-s{color:#1c1b18;font-weight:700}.ds-del{background:#f3f0e8;color:#6b6559}.ds-del span:last-child{text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-color:color-mix(in oklab,#6b6559 45%,transparent)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Case File",
    "overview": "Every finding on this page has already stood before a tribunal: Verification tried to refute it, or Judgment decided to keep it. The page is the file that hearing left behind. A kraft folder with a tabbed spine holds a ruled index sheet and a run of bond-paper exhibit sheets, each carrying its claim on the left and its evidence clipped on the right. Adjudication is a rubber stamp, review is a stamp you press yourself, and what the tribunal threw out hangs in a set-aside sleeve at the back.\n\nThe world is dense and quiet. One warm, ruled neutral ramp carries everything; type does the hierarchy work in a single variable grotesk, condensed for anything that reads as a printed form field and set at normal width for prose. Colour is never decoration and never syntax: it appears only as the ink a priority was stamped in. The page refuses the dashboard-plus-card-feed and the GitHub diff clone; it is a file you read, not a console you monitor.\n\nIt is one offline HTML file per Run, deterministic from `dossier.json` and git, with an optional agent-authored brief clipped to Judgment-path exhibits. Both are drawn by the same renderer from the same typed blocks.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Kraft spine, bond sheets, desk underneath: three paper layers, no other surfaces.",
      "One variable grotesk (Archivo) at two widths, plus mono only for code.",
      "Colour is adjudication ink only: P1, P2, P3 and the Gauntlet mark.",
      "Priority reads three ways at once: stamp size, the P-label, and ink.",
      "Every exhibit's tag pins to its cited line by a dashed leader rule.",
      "One authored motion: the reviewed stamp pressing onto the sheet."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Adjudication Ink Rule",
        "body": "Hue appears only where a tribunal ruled: the stamp, the spine's P-chip, the docket count, the cited-line mark and its pin, and the accent strokes of a diagram drawn inside that exhibit. Each exhibit sets one `--ink` from its priority and everything inside it draws from that one variable. If a colour is not a priority's ink or the Gauntlet mark, it is a neutral from the ramp.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hue-Free Evidence Rule",
        "body": "Syntax highlighting and diff bands carry no hue. Keywords are carbon at weight 650, types at 550, strings a step softer, comments Ink 3 in italic. An added row is a neutral band with a bold `+`; a removed row is a paler band with struck-through Ink 3 text. Green and red would compete with priority, and priority wins.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bond-Paper Ink Rule",
        "body": "The dark theme uses the Mod strip's priority inks exactly. On light bond paper the inks shift darker (`#d93b40`, `#e57a00`, `#b98f00`) because the strip's values wash out on paper: P1 rises from 3.62:1 to 4.18:1 against Bond, P2 from 2.23:1 to 2.73:1, P3 from 1.87:1 to 2.78:1. That gain is real but P2 and P3 still sit under 3:1, so priority must never rest on hue alone: the stamp size ramp and the printed `P2`/`P3` label carry it too.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Form-Field Rule",
        "body": "Anything that names a field, files an exhibit or rules on it is condensed uppercase. Anything that argues is full-width sentence case. Never set prose condensed or labels at full width.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Count Rule",
        "body": "Every count (docket, spine tabs, cost, invocations, reviewed progress, line numbers) uses tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper-Only Rule",
        "body": "Three surfaces exist: desk, kraft, bond. A new surface is one of those or a Bond Under inset inside a sheet.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** set one `--ink` per exhibit from its priority and draw every hued element inside it from that variable.",
      "**Do** size stamps only on the ramp: 25px P1, 20px P2, 16px P3, 14px unranked.",
      "**Do** keep evidence hue-free: weight, italic, Ink 3, neutral bands and strike-through carry syntax and diff meaning.",
      "**Do** use the strip's exact inks (`#e5484d`, `#ff8700`, `#e0b000`) on dark paper and the shifted bond-paper inks (`#d93b40`, `#e57a00`, `#b98f00`) on light.",
      "**Do** set field labels, tabs, tags, stamps and actions condensed uppercase, and prose at full width in sentence case.",
      "**Do** add new agent-authored content as one of the six typed blocks.",
      "**Do** keep motion to the reviewed-stamp press and the sleeve chevron, and honour `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** colour syntax tokens or diff rows; no green additions, no red deletions.",
      "**Don't** introduce a colour that is not a priority ink, the Gauntlet mark or a ramp neutral.",
      "**Don't** let an agent supply HTML, CSS, colour or layout; it supplies blocks.",
      "**Don't** let priority rest on hue alone; every inked element also carries its P-label or its place on the size ramp.",
      "**Don't** add a surface beyond desk, kraft, bond and a Bond Under inset, and don't lift sheets on hover.",
      "**Don't** stamp anything decorative; a stamp, flag or clip always marks a state."
    ]
  }
}
